.TH edgo 3 "2026-08-03"
.SH NAME
edgo \- text editor library with native lsp support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <edgo.h>
.SH MODULE OVERVIEW
.SS Screen printing functions
Functions that are manipulating the text buffer while printing the screen content as a return value.
.TP
char* \f3add_text\fP(size_t \fIline\fP, size_t \fIpos\fP, const char* \fIbuf\fP, size_t \fIlength\fP);
Adds character or text to the buffer.
.TP
char* \f3remove_text\fP(size_t \fIline\fP, size_t \fIpos\fP, size_t \fIlength\fP);
Removes character or text from the buffer.
.TP
char* \f3replace_text\fP(size_t \fIline\fP, size_t \fIfrom\fP, size_t \fIend\fP, const char* \fIbuf\fP, size_t \fIlength\fP);
Replaces text between ranges.
.TP
char* \f3shift_with_tabs\fP(size_t \fIline\fP, size_t \fIpos\fP, int* \fIarr\fP, size_t \fIarr_len\fP);
Shifting with tabs to the right using integer array of lines.
.TP
char* \f3display_screen_report\fP(const char* \fIdirpath\fP, size_t \fIlength\fP);
Displaying screen report of the current working folder.
.TP
char* \f3clipboard\fP(enum clipboard_ops \fIops\fP);
Clipboard operations are handled according the parameter.
.TP
char* \f3duplicate\fP(void);
Duplicates the currently selected line under cursor.
.TP
char* \f3commentline\fP(void);
Adds comment character(s) to the beginning of the line.
.TP
char* \f3swaplinesup\fP(void);
Moves current line up under the cursor.
.TP
char* \f3swaplinesdn\fP(void);
Moves current line down under the cursor.
.SS Navigation keys
Methods return screen output while handling navigation.
.TP
char* \f3on_keypress\fP(enum nav_keys \fIkeys\fP, void* \fIis_paging\fP);
Handles key presses according to the parameter.
.TP
char* \f3on_scroll\fP(enum nav_keys \fIkeys\fP);
This method is only for UP and DOWN scrolling for mouse inputs.
.SS File operations
All file operations have to be handled at the start as they are initializing the library.
.TP
char* \f3open_file\fP(const char* \fIfilepath\fP);
Opens file providing the file path in the argument.
.TP
int \f3new_file\fP(const char* \fIfilename\fP);
Creates a new file in the current working directory by providing the name only.
.TP
int \f3save_file\fP(void);
Saves the file currently being opened.
.SS LSP client functions
Commands initiated by the user for interaction with the language server.
.TP
void \f3lsp_client_hover\fP(struct lsp_hover*);
Displays information when hovering the cursor under a text.
.TP
void \f3lsp_client_completion\fP(struct lsp_completion*);
Provides auto-complete suggestions.
.TP
void \f3lsp_client_definition\fP(struct lsp_definition*);
Jumps to the definition or declaration under the cursor.
.TP
void \f3lsp_client_signature_help\fP(struct lsp_signature_help*);
Displays signature information of the current method.
.TP
void \f3lsp_client_references\fP(struct lsp_references*);
Retrieves the list of references in the working directory.
.TP
void \f3lsp_client_prepare_rename\fP(struct lsp_prepare_rename*);
Determines if a symbol can be renamed safely before it is being renamed.
.TP
void \f3lsp_client_rename\fP(const char* \fInewname\fP, struct lsp_rename*);
Renames a symbol under cursor.
.TP
void \f3lsp_client_code_action\fP(struct lsp_code_action*);
Returns a list of possible actions for the file being opened.
.SS LSP diagnostics
This command has to be issued whenever the user needs diagnostics.
.TP
void \f3lsp_diagnostics\fP(struct lsp_publish_diagnostics*);
Retrieves diagnostics from the currently opened file.
.SH PARAMETERS
.TP
\f2ops\fP
Specifies the clipboard buffer operation.
Symbolic constants
\%\f3COPY\fP,
\%\f3PASTE\fP,
\%\f3CUT\fP,
\%\f3UNDO\fP,
and
\%\f3REDO\fP are accepted.
.TP
\f2keys\fP
Specifies the navigation keys pressed such as
\%\f3UP\fP,
\%\f3DOWN\fP,
\%\f3LEFT\fP,
\%\f3RIGHT\fP,
\%\f3TOP\fP,
\%\f3BOTTOM\fP,
\%\f3ENTER\fP,
\%\f3DEL\fP,
\%\f3TAB\fP,
\%\f3BACKTAB\fP.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Edgo is a library for text editors providing syntax highlighting and language server protocol (LSP).
It is also providing functionality for text manipulation, search, selection and language queries.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Edgo uses EDGO_CONF and EDGO_LOG environment variables to alter the editor behaviour or to produce
diagnostic logs for debugging. Once the config file path is set you can change themes for the editor
and configure custom LSP servers. Please note however we aim to provide builtin LSP server configurations
for every languages that are supported by the editor.
.SH THEMES
A set of themes are included in the editor and available to be changed in the configuration file.
Some of the themes are darcula, edgo, edgo-new, material-darker, vesper.
.SH LSP SUPPORT
Following lsp features are supported: completion, hover, signature help, definition,
references, rename, method extraction and diagnostic information.
.PP
Install your language server for interaction with your text editor.
.SH SYNTAX HIGHLIGHTING
Following languages are currently supported: bash, c/c++, go, html, css, java, javascript,
typescript, python and rust
